    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0935" n="923" xml:id="pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.51/12–1246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-12-12T18:00:00-05:00">December 12,
                            1946—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>804. For Ambassador from Henderson: My letter and memo Nov 7<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d729-f1"/> represent in very broad terms what we would like to
                    accomplish whereas Deptel 784<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d729-f2"/> referring specifically to additional Eximbank loan illustrates practical
                    difficulties confronting us particularly in dealing with independent agencies.
                        (Embtel 1249 Dec 10<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d729-f3"/>) We still hope that Eximbank will alter attitude re additional loan. In any event we
                    are continuing to explore possibilities for effective economic aid. Your
                    suggestions will be welcomed.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d729-f4"/> [Henderson.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d729-f1" n="62" xml:id="d729-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 12, <ref target="#pg894">p. 894</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d729-f2" n="63" xml:id="d729-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 55, <ref target="#pg921">p. 921</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d729-f3" n="64" xml:id="d729-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; it asked for clarification, as in the letter of December 7, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d729-f4" n="65" xml:id="d729-f4-content">
                <p>In telegram 1256, December 16, 1 p.m., from Ankara, the Ambassador said he hoped
                    the information sent “will be helpful to Department in considering question of
                    economic aid to Turkey”. (867.51/12–1646)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
